# OpenFrame: no vendor and model name tables in udev's hardware database (about 20 MB with the
# compiled database, which udev reads at every start). They only put names to vendors and
# models; lsusb and lspci fall back to what each device says of itself. The rest of the
# database (keyboards, sensors, touchscreens) stays. openframe-scripts' postinst removes them
# once from a system that has them, and rebuilds the database.
path-exclude=/usr/lib/udev/hwdb.d/20-*.hwdb
